{"change_summary":"No additional source edits were required in this apply-fixes pass. The approved carbonate-equilibrium rollout was already present in the worktree, including the explicit solver-driven pH path, save-load carbonate cache normalization, preset validation, and the daily shrimp-path carbonate refresh, so this stage verified the integrated state rather than patching code again.","outstanding_risks":["`solve_carbonate_equilibrium()` still uses an aquarium-focused approximation with fixed `Ka2`, so any future extension beyond the intended freshwater pH 5.5-8.5 envelope should revisit the chemistry model.","The unrelated untracked `.ralph-burning/` directory remains in the worktree and was left untouched."],"steps":[{"description":"Review the prior apply-fixes and validation outputs, then inspect the current worktree for unresolved carbonate follow-up items.","order":0,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Apply any remaining carbonate-solver follow-up fixes; skipped because the review approved the implementation with no actionable amendments.","order":1,"status":"skipped"},{"description":"Re-run regression and quality checks to confirm the approved carbonate/state-contract implementation remains green in the current workspace.","order":2,"status":"completed"}],"validation_evidence":["`git status --short` showed no tracked source deltas; only the unrelated untracked `.ralph-burning/` directory is present.","`cargo test -p tank_core` passed, including chemistry, save/load, shrimp-feeding-pathway, shrimp-population, substrate/filter integration, and end-to-end coverage.","`cargo test -p tank_data --lib` passed (4 tests), including shipped source-water carbonate differentiation and out-of-range carbonate pH rejection.","`cargo fmt --all --check` passed.","`cargo clippy -p tank_core -p tank_data --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed."]}